      "id": "0ba1998b-9e10-4676-9b65-f0fa593da36b",
      "name": "IF - Renewal Within 30 Days?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        128,
        112
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Subscription: {{ $json.SubscriptionName }} ({{ $json.Vendor }})\nOwner: {{ $json.OwnerName }}\nRenews in: {{ $json.DaysUntilRenewal }} days\nMonthly cost: ${{ $json.MonthlyCost }}\nLicensed seats: {{ $('Get Subscriptions').item.json.LicensedSeats }}\nActive users (last 30 days): {{ $('Get Subscriptions').item.json.ActiveUsers }}\nUtilization: {{ $json.UtilizationPct }}%\nDays since last use: {{ $('Calculate Renewal & Usage Status').item.json.DaysSinceLastUsed }}\nLooks unused: {{ $json.IsUnused }}\n\nWrite the body of a short internal note to Finance about this upcoming renewal. If \"Looks unused\" is true, be direct that usage data suggests this subscription may not be needed anymore and recommend reviewing whether to cancel before it renews - state the utilization numbers plainly. If \"Looks unused\" is false, keep it brief and low-key: just a heads-up that it's renewing soon and usage looks healthy, no action implied. 3-5 sentences, plain English, no headers, no markdown, ready to drop into an HTML email paragraph.",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are a SaaS spend review assistant. You write concise, factual notes for a Finance team about upcoming software renewals. You never invent numbers - you only use the figures given to you. You are direct about likely-unused subscriptions but never alarmist, and neutral/brief about subscriptions that are clearly still in active use."
        }
      },
